  "enhanced_information": "For the elderly population infected with a thymidine kinase-deficient varicella-zoster virus strain causing shingles, acyclovir may have reduced efficacy due to the virus strain's reduced susceptibility. Famciclovir may also be less effective due to potential cross-resistance with acyclovir. Ganciclovir is not recommended as the virus strain lacks thymidine kinase. Cidofovir could be considered as it does not require viral thymidine kinase for activation. Amantadine, targeting a different viral protein, might also be a potential option. Evidence paths support the use of acyclovir, famciclovir, ganciclovir, cidofovir, and amantadine in treating herpes zoster disease caused by the virus."
